        "summary": "Provider - Update",
        "description": "Partial update — config fields only. Accepts any subset of: name, feed_url, capture_node, username, password, refresh_minutes, schema_mapping, click_id_param, job_partner_id, fetch_method, fetch_config, fetch_credentials. To toggle pause/resume/active-state, use the dedicated action endpoints.\n\n`fetch_config` REPLACES the stored object wholesale — send the complete config, not a partial patch. When `fetch_method` is present the config is validated against the new method; when it is absent the CURRENT stored method is used, so you can PATCH config alone without restating the method.\n\nSend `fetch_credentials: null` to CLEAR stored credentials (the correct move after switching a provider to `credential_source: \"instance\"`). Omitting the field leaves them untouched.",
